{
 "summary": "Modify `node::GetTransaction` and `TxIndex` methods to throw `std::runtime_error` on block data I/O failures, deserialization errors, and index corruption instead of treating them as missing transactions. Update `getrawtransaction` to call `CheckBlockDataAvailability` on errors to provide explicit error messages for pruned or downloading blocks, and consolidate `ProcessPSBT` lookups to use `GetTransaction` directly.",
 "problem": "When disk reads fail due to I/O errors, block file corruption, or index database corruption, `GetTransaction` and `TxIndex` return null or empty results. Callers like `getrawtransaction`, `gettxoutproof`, and `/rest/tx/` misinterpret this as a nonexistent transaction and report it as missing, misleading users and masking disk corruption.",
 "evidence": [
  "Commit `fad44f18b8`: 'When a block hash is passed in and the block can't be read, the RPC reports \"No such transaction found in the provided block\", even though the block was never searched. Fix this by throwing an I/O error from GetTransaction when ReadBlock fails.'",
  "Commit `fa12509a47`: '...a -txindex corruption may also point to a larger system corruption and it seems better to notify the user properly by throwing an exception.'"
 ],
